        heading: 'Specific performance in respect of contracts',
        text: 'The specific performance of a contract shall be enforced by the court subject to the provisions contained in sub-section (2) of section 11, section 14 and section 16. [Note: as substituted by the Specific Relief (Amendment) Act, 2018 (with effect from 1 October 2018) — this replaced the earlier position under which specific performance was granted only "in the discretion of the court" and only where damages would not be an adequate remedy. It is now the default remedy for breach of contract, subject only to the specific bars in sections 11(2), 14, and 16, not a court\'s general discretion. This directly affects how a breach-of-contract claim under the Indian Contract Act, 1872 (sections 73–74 in this Library) is pleaded — a claimant is no longer required to show that damages would be inadequate before seeking performance instead.]',
