        text: '(1) This Act may be called the Punjab Courts Act, 1918. (2) Haryana continued to apply this common Act — the same one that applied to undivided Punjab — after its creation as a separate state in 1966; no separate Haryana-specific Courts Act or amending Act altering its pecuniary-jurisdiction provisions was found. A search of India Code did not surface any distinct "Haryana Courts Act" or Haryana amendment to sections 25 or 26 of this Act.',
