        sectionNo: '25',
        heading: 'Original jurisdiction of District Judge in suits',
        text: 'Except as otherwise provided by any enactment for the time being in force, the Court of the District Judge shall have jurisdiction in every original civil suit the value of which does not exceed rupees twenty lakhs. [Note: as with Punjab, this ₹20 lakh figure (Central Act No. 35 of 2003, effective 16 July 2003) is a ceiling on the District Judge\'s own original jurisdiction, not a floor above which a suit must be filed before the District Judge. Civil Judges (Senior Division) can independently be classified with unlimited pecuniary jurisdiction under section 26, so most higher-value money recovery suits in Haryana are in practice filed before a Civil Judge, not the District Judge.]',
